  m_IsActive: 1
--- !u!114 &1762714893
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1762714892}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 51bf743a7b9a61e409329faa416e2f81, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Ronin7.World::Ronin7.World.Story.DialoguePlayer
  lines:
  - speaker: Dr. Heris
    text: From the bigger thing they made me build next. They saw what the suppression
      science could do to one mind and they were not satisfied with one. They took
      my work, all of it, and they conscripted me to scale it. Not a leash for an
      operative. A voice for the sky. The Concord Engine. One transmitter, tuned
      to the same science that sits in your skull, built to reach every mind on every
      world at once and tell it to be quiet. To stop. To obey. I built that too.
      Under threat, which is not an excuse, only a fact.
    seconds: 39
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8d053a72f935c7a418ab915b46e47438, type: 3}
  - speaker: Ronin-7
    text: You built a machine to silence every world at once. Tell me you didn't
      make it perfect. Tell me you cracked this one too.
    seconds: 9
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6596a0063fc806a47bc0dd36618eee70, type: 3}
  - speaker: Dr. Heris
    text: I did the only thing a coward with a conscience can do. I built it perfectly,
      and then I hid a flaw in it. The same kind of seam I hid in you. One deniable
      gap, in the one machine that could silence everything. And I have held the
      location of that gap, alone, in my own head, for years, on the single chance
      that the man I broke open would survive long enough to come back and let me
      give it to him.
    seconds: 33
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e6b19298b6084684d9e3d69fc5456249, type: 3}
  - speaker: Echo
    text: There it is, Cipher. The seam Sable said she couldn't feel from the ship.
      The one soft spot on the whole machine. It's not on the machine. It's in her
      head. She built the only weakness it has and she's been carrying it like a
      held breath waiting for you. Whatever you feel about everything else she just
      said, and I feel all of it too, that's the thing the crew needs. The Engine
      has a flaw, and she is the flaw.
    seconds: 31
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 0ee744a297cc66647a163aaa7dc95af0, type: 3}
  textMesh: {fileID: 1631833009}
  panelRoot: {fileID: 186636610}
  audioSource: {fileID: 1762714894}
  billboardToCamera: 1
  playOnStart: 0
  followDistance: 1.5
  followVerticalOffset: -0.55
